The (reported) change in sales is a relative indicator.It shows the percentage by which sales varied from the previous year.The currency-adjusted or currency- and portfolio-adjusted change in sales shows the percentage change in sales excluding the impact of exchange rate effects and, in the latter case, disregarding material acquisitions and divestments as well.Exchange rate effects are generally calculated on the basis of the functional currency valid in the respective country.An exception existed in Argentina, primarily in our crop protection business, where the currency effect was calculated on the basis of the US dollar instead of the functional currency.

